Inspiration only, nothing copied: the upstream cache engine budgets its KV
memory from the rows it actually keeps — owner-layer compressed rows plus
indexer keys, with the per-layer device row mirror accounted per layer —
instead of a uniform per-token product. Fak's DeepSeek-V4.1 context plan
under FAK_HYBRID_KV (#13914) takes that kept-KV accounting shape: each
decoder layer's bounded window mirror is charged per layer, the published
compressed rows and index keys ride their source layers' entries, and the
compressor's in-flight rows are charged once in session state. No upstream
type, constant, or logic was ported; the arithmetic is fak's own
(compute.CompressedKVLayer over the published retention schedule).
